&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-.5in;text-align:justify'>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>            Since the nature of mankind is a central
consideration in Christian theology, the doctrine of natural depravity in mankind
affects a variety of issues and impacts them in significant ways. The following
enumeration of consequences may not be necessary in every case, but historically
this concept has triggered them. &lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>PREVENIENT GRACE AND NATURAL DEPRAVITY</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/depravity/prevenient-grace-and-natural-depravity/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/depravity/prevenient-grace-and-natural-depravity/</guid><description>&lt;style>
