the fall was any different from what it was (4) &lt;u>before the fall&lt;/u> in a (5)
&lt;u>biologically&lt;/u> inheritable sense. &lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>STATES OF MAN AND IMPLICATIONS FOR DEPRAVITY IN ROMANS 7 AND 8</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/depravity/states-of-man-and-implications-for-depravity-in-romans-7-and-8/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/mankind-anthropology/depravity/states-of-man-and-implications-for-depravity-in-romans-7-and-8/</guid><description>&lt;style>
